(EXP-85: the casting Examples block at LANGUAGE.md:2090-2108 compiles verbatim
 and gives the documented results.
 Also covers: EXP-86, the inline cast `Print 3.14159 as a number`, which is the
 block's last line and the one form that casts in argument position rather
 than in an initializer.
 The manual's own names are kept, quoted names included: `pi` is a legal
 variable name and `'pi truncated'` and `'done num'` are legal quoted ones.
 Only the four Print lines are added.
